  "notes": {
   "wall_*_intact": "exactly fills [0,W]x[0,H]x[-T,0] -> game normalisation offset is zero",
   "damage_states": "all four states share the intact frame; damaged/holed/destroyed may protrude to +Z (curtains, rebar, door leaves, balcony stub) and -Z (room-side debris, radiators) by design",
   "wall_balcony_holed": "includes the broken-off root of the balcony slab (game removes balcony_slab at state>=2)",
   "balcony_slab": "mixed corrugated asbestos parapet + residents' glazing (wood/PVC/boarded). Variants balcony_slab_open, balcony_slab_glazed are extra (same placement rules) for the game to randomise",
   "balcony_hanging": "hinge (wall face, slab top) is at local y = bbox_max.y - 0.14 relative to bbox min; game normalises minY=0 so place it at floor_y - (bbox height - 0.14) to keep the hinge at the slab line",
   "entrance_canopy": "slab bottom at bbox minY+0.06 (lamp housing hangs 6 cm below the slab)",
   "roof_parapet": "height 0.72 m + galvanised cap; roofing upturn on the room side (-Z)",
   "slab_floor": "3.2 x 0.22 x 3.2 m (x, y, -z). Top = linoleum, bottom = whitewashed ceiling. slab_floor_broken: outer half hinged down 35 deg on its bottom rebar",
   "stair_core": "3.2 wide x 2.8 high x 4.5 deep: flight up from z=-4.2 (floor landing provided by slab_floor) to the half-landing at y=1.4 against the facade, second flight back up to y=2.8",
   "plinth": "3.2 x 0.9 x 0.45 basement plinth with vent grille, same pivot rules as walls",
   "partition_wall_*": "interior gypsum partition 3.2 x 2.58 x 0.08 with doorway; _intact/_holed",
   "debris_*": "loose furniture debris (wardrobe, bed, table+chair, radiator), origin on the floor",
   "brick_<type>_<state>, brick_red_<type>_<state>": "series 1-447 brick walls, types window/balcony/blank_end/entrance, same 3.2 x 2.8 x 0.3 frame, openings and 4 damage states as wall_*; brick_* = white silicate brick, brick_red_* = red ceramic brick (two piece sets, same geometry, different atlas cells). Reuse balcony_slab*/entrance_canopy/plinth. Holes are stair-stepped along the brick courses; masonry mesh wires instead of rebar",
   "brick_parapet, brick_red_parapet": "brick roof parapet 0.69 m with corbelled course + galvanised cap; wall frame (maxZ = 0)",
   "wall_shopfront_<state>, wall_shopfront_shutter_<state>": "ground-floor shop panel (converted flat): tiled piers + glazed door + 2x2 display window / one wide opening with a steel roller shutter (closed when intact, half-raised and torn when damaged, ripped out when holed). Fascia y 2.08..2.8 is left for a sign_* piece. Same frame and states as wall_*",
   "sign_<shop>_intact|_damaged": "shop sign mounted on the fascia: place in panel coords with its bottom at y = 2.14 on a wall_shopfront* panel. Authored in the accessory frame (centred on x = W/2, starts at the wall face z = 0, extends +Z up to 0.17) -> normalise like balcony/entrance_canopy (add ^sign_ to the accessory regex in buildKit). Shops: apteka, produkty, khlib, magazyn, perukarnia, gospodarchi, kafe, kvity, ovochi, zootovary. _damaged = right bracket torn, hanging tilted (shares the _intact offset)",
   "roof_machine_room, roof_vent, roof_antenna": "roof-top pieces, origin at their footprint centre on the roof surface (y = 0), +Z front (machine-room door). Place on the roof slab of 9+ storey blocks (machine room above a stair core). buildKit normalises them to minX=0/minY=0/maxZ=0: add bbox_min.x / bbox_max.z back to recentre",
   "collapse_pile_large, collapse_pile_small": "section-collapse rubble: pancaked floor slabs on a rubble mound with rebar, standing facade remnants, leaning/lying panels, balcony, furniture. Origin = footprint centre on the ground, +Z = side the section fell towards (street). large ~13 x 13 m, small ~7 x 7 m (see bbox)",
   "slab_hanging": "slab_floor frame (x 0..3.2, -z inward): floor slab of the storey above hanging diagonally from its interior support line (hinge = slab top at y = H, z = -W) down to the floor below (free edge y ~ 0.05, z ~ -1.6). With the generic minX/minY/maxZ normalisation the hinge sits at (x, H - bbox_min.y, -W - bbox_max.z)"
  }
 },
